Z||000000||Ronen||05-09-2001||04:20 PM||||I just bought my first Fiero on April 16th 2001 for $1400.00. It has a sunroof, A/C, power locks and windows. It is a V6 85 GT. It was built on 6/85. Grey in color. This past weekend while driving by the Columbia River in Oregon A black Fiero GT w/ a rear wing original spoiler caught my eye at a towing company. I stoped by and ask how much for the spoiler. Expecting to hear the usual $300-$400 I was stunned to hear $150.00 for the wing and I can take the car, too. So, since I work for a towing company I will have one of the drivers get it to me. The selling outfit does not know how to repair it so they do not know why it was abandoned on the road. It has the original radio which I am missing and two seats with minor cuts in them. Mine has no fabric on the seat. So I will be replacing many many parts and the engine I would like to keep but my father in law says sell the scrap with the engine at least so it has some value. He is a mechanic. What is the going rate on a beat up Fiero V6 that does not run. The guys at work say that a lot of people abandon cars due to runing out of fuel. Wouldn't that be beautifull?||||reg||5
